What this covers
----------------

CC0 applies to the solid-panes registry contents:

  - <Name>/index.json              — each manifest (urn:solid type → pane + schema)
  - schema/manifest.schema.json    — meta-schema enforcing manifest shape
  - corpus.jsonl                   — generated: every manifest as one record per line
  - index.json                     — generated: name → manifest summary
  - reverse-index.json             — generated: urn:solid type → manifest URL

What this does NOT cover
------------------------

Code in this repository remains licensed under AGPL-3.0 (see LICENSE):

  - scripts/*.js
  - auto-schema.js                 — opt-in helper that patches $schema based on @type
  - schema-view.js                 — read-only counterpart to LOSOS's schema-pane
  - generated <Name>/index.html, top-level index.html, demo/

Why
---

Manifests are pointers — knowing "urn:solid:Person → this pane URL +
this schema URL" should be friction-free for any consumer to use.
CC0 on the manifests means downstream apps and registries can republish
them without inheriting copyleft. The actual pane code (auto-schema,
schema-view) stays AGPL because that's where the implementation lives.
